<title>SWITZERLAND: Maag sells U.S. unit to Textron.</title>
<headline>Maag sells U.S. unit to Textron.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Maag Holding AG said it had sold its Burkland Holding Inc unit to Textron Inc. It gave no financial details.</p>
<p>Burkland, which makes components for the North American automobile industry, generated 1996 sales of 20 million Swiss francs and employed 109 people, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>The transaction marked another step in Maag's withdrawal from industrial activity, it said.</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom +41 1 631 7340</p>
